Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 15 — XML View-Based Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to systematically understand traditional Android applications built using the View System and XML layouts. Before Jetpack Compose, nearly every Android app used this architecture, and many enterprise and legacy applications still do. By the end of this section, you should be able to reconstruct UI architecture, layout inflation, view hierarchies, event propagation, rendering, resource resolution, and the interaction between XML and Java/Kotlin code.



> Core Principle:
In XML-based applications, the UI exists in two worlds: XML describes the structure, while Java/Kotlin defines the behavior. Reverse engineer both together.




