Stage 28 — Common XML Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Reading XML without correlating it to Java/Kotlin.

Ignoring View lifecycle.

Treating RecyclerView as ordinary layouts.

Confusing generated ViewBinding/DataBinding code with handwritten logic.

Ignoring theme and style inheritance.

Following UI implementation before understanding navigation architecture.



---

Stage 29 — XML View Application Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify XML View-based Android applications and reconstruct their UI architecture.

✅ Recover Activities, Fragments, View hierarchies, navigation, and rendering pipelines.

✅ Understand layout inflation, resource resolution, themes, ViewBinding, and DataBinding.

✅ Trace user interactions from touch events through business logic and back to UI updates.

✅ Distinguish generated UI infrastructure from handwritten presentation logic.

✅ Validate reconstructed UI behavior through runtime observation.

✅ Produce comprehensive documentation describing the complete presentation architecture and its interaction with the rest of the application.



